Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-09 Task 2 — primitive numeric cross-casts. Without these
Note: strict-mode composers have no escape hatch for cross-type comparisons:
Note: `(double 1)` would fail overload resolution because Int → Double widening
Note: is disabled under strict (Plan 44-03). Each of the 4 extractors accepts
Note: every primitive numeric source. Narrowing floors per StdLib.DoubleToInt
Note: convention.
Note:
Note: Phase 44 review WR-05: identity casts ((double Double), (float Float),
Note: (int Int), (long Long)) are intentionally OMITTED. They were no-ops
Note: with no strict-mode ambiguity to escape, added overload-resolution
Note: competitors for no benefit, and risked silent shadowing of other Double-
Note: source overloads under strict. The 12 cross-type rows below cover every
Note: case where strict mode disables the widening implicit-conversion.
internal proc double (Int: value)
internal proc double (Long: value)
internal proc double (Float: value)

internal proc float (Int: value)
internal proc float (Long: value)
internal proc float (Double: value)

internal proc int (Long: value)
internal proc int (Float: value)
internal proc int (Double: value)

internal proc long (Int: value)
internal proc long (Float: value)
internal proc long (Double: value)

